    "summary": "Capital Centre ’82 debuts Touch of Grey with a blistering Play‑in > Crazy Fingers ride",
    "review": "What unfolds at the Capital Centre on September 15, 1982 is a landmark night that still feels fresh for any Deadhead. The band launches into an electrifying “Playing In The Band → Crazy Fingers” sequence that sets a high‑octane tone and never lets up, weaving through jams that feel like a second set even before the official one begins. Brent Mydland’s keyboards are in top form, adding texture to the Let It Grow and Shakedown Street explosions, while Jerry’s noodling on those tunes is nothing short of inspired. The second set keeps the momentum with a powerhouse run of Lost Sailor → Saint Of Circumstance, a thunderous drum duet, and soaring renditions of Not Fade Away, Stella Blue and Good Lovin’. The night caps off with an emotional encore – the first ever live Touch of Grey – delivering a historic moment that still resonates. Across the board the performances are tight, the transitions seamless, and the energy consistently high, making this show one of the most compelling snapshots of the early‑’80s Dead.",
